Validation failed for tool "ask_user_questions":
  - questions: must be array

Received arguments:
{
  "questions": "[{\"id\": \"ci_failure_handling\", \"header\": \"CI Failure Mode\", \"question\": \"How should we handle test failures in CI? Currently || true swallows them.\", \"options\": [{\"label\": \"Fail on real failures (Recommended)\", \"description\": \"Remove || true from CI. Unit tests fail the build. Integration tests use a separate conditional gate.\"}, {\"label\": \"Fail everything including infra tests\", \"description\": \"Remove || true everywhere. If any test anywhere fails, the build is red regardless of why.\"}]}, {\"id\": \"test_separation\", \"header\": \"Test Separation\", \"question\": \"How should we separate unit from integration tests in CI?\", \"options\": [{\"label\": \"Marker-based split (Recommended)\", \"description\": \"Run unit tests (default, no marker needed) in a fast CI job, then run @pytest.mark.integration tests in a separate job with services. No service spin-up unless integration tests run.\"}, {\"label\": \"Directory-based split\", \"description\": \"Move integration tests into tests/integration/, unit tests stay in tests/. Two pytest invocations. Cleaner separation but more file moves.\"}]}, {\"label\": \"CI with services always\", \"description\": \"Keep current pattern — all tests in one pass with Postgres/Redis/Qdrant always running. Just remove || true so failures surface.\"}, {\"label\": \"Local runner + CI\", \"description\": \"Add a Makefile with 'make test-unit' and 'make test-integration' targets. CI uses the same targets. Integration tests get a marker-based skip when infra isn't available locally.\"}]}, {\"id\": \"coverage_fix\", \"header\": \"Coverage Config\", \"question\": \"The coverage source path points to src/ but the package finder points elsewhere. How should we fix it?\", \"options\": [{\"label\": \"Fix source to the actual package dir (Recommended)\", \"description\": \"Set coverage source to the actual heretek_swarm package location (where __init__.py lives). This makes coverage accurate.\"}, {\"label\": \"Fix both to match 'src' layout\", \"description\": \"Configure setuptools to the src-layout pattern properly. Cleaner but involves pyproject.toml surgery.\"}]}]"
}
